.TH HD-LAPTOP 7 "November 2026" "hd-laptop" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-laptop \- the parts of HyprDebian for laptops
.SH DESCRIPTION
The package
.B hd-laptop
holds the parts of HyprDebian that only laptops need.
It depends on
.BR hd-desktop (7),
as its notifications are shown by mako in the desktop session.
.SS Battery
.BR hd-battery (1)
shows the level of the battery in a notification, with the time left until
it is empty or full.
The key binding
.B SUPER + SHIFT + B
runs it.
.PP
The user unit
.B hd-battery-monitor.service
runs
.B hd-battery \-\-monitor
in the desktop session, which shows a notification when the battery falls to
50%, 25%, 10% and 5% on battery power, and when the charger is plugged in or
pulled out.
The package enables the unit for every user on its first installation; it
starts at the next login.
Its messages are in the journal of the user:
.PP
.RS
.B journalctl --user -u hd-battery-monitor
.RE
.PP
To turn it off for a user:
.PP
.RS
.B systemctl --user disable --now hd-battery-monitor
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/hd-battery
Shows the battery level, and watches the battery with
.BR \-\-monitor .
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/hd-battery-monitor.service
The user unit that watches the battery.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-battery (1),
.BR hd-desktop (7)
